    "badge": "Best Value",
    "category": "Inflatable, All-Around, 11 ft",
    "description": "The Atoll 11 is the value pick: an 11 ft board with a capacity high enough for larger riders, at a lower price than the premium kits. Reviewers measured it at 11 ft long, 32 in wide and 6 in thick, with a board weight of 21 lb and a full kit weight of 38 lb including accessories. Reviewers list a maximum capacity of 315 lb; one retailer claims 400 lb, which conflicts with the reviewers' figure, so plan around 315 lb. One reviewer noted that the 15 PSI maximum rating is not quite enough to keep the board fully stiff when sprinting, which is a fair trade at this price for casual paddling but worth knowing if you want a very rigid board. The kit includes a pump, a three-piece paddle and a travel backpack, and one spec table lists a two-year warranty. Weight figures vary between 19 and 21 lb across model years, so check the current listing.",
