    ],
    "bottomLine": "An 11 ft board with a higher capacity than most at a value price."
  },
  {
    "id": "bote-breeze-aero-10-8",
    "name": "BOTE Breeze Aero 10'8\"",
    "badge": "Best for Beginners",
    "category": "Inflatable, All-Around, 10 ft 8 in",
    "description": "The Breeze Aero is a friendly, well-made board for beginners and lighter paddlers who value easy handling. Retailer and review sources agree on a length of 10 ft 8 in, a width of 33 in, a thickness of 6 in, a capacity of 250 lb and a board weight of about 20 lb. BOTE lists an optimal inflation of 10 to 15 PSI, and the travel bag packs down to about 38 by 18 by 12 in with a loaded weight of 26 lb. Retailers list a removable 10 in center fin, a repair kit, a hand pump and a travel bag in the box, and one adds a three-piece adjustable paddle. BOTE's own sizing advice is useful: if your weight is within 50 lb of a board's listed capacity, BOTE recommends moving up to a larger board, which for this model means riders above about 200 lb should look at the 11 ft 6 in version, listed at 315 lb. Some listings mix up a 10 ft 6 in variant, so check the exact length before you buy.",
