          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For most paddlers, the <strong class="text-white">Isle Pioneer 3</strong> is the board to buy: stable, light and sold with a carbon paddle and a wheeled bag. Heavier riders should start with the <strong class="text-white">Gili Meno</strong>, and the <strong class="text-white">Atoll 11</strong> is the value pick with a higher capacity than most.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Size the board to your weight, inflate it to the recommended pressure, wear a leash and a life jacket, and start out into the wind. Those four habits matter more than which brand you choose.
          </p>
